FerrionOS change to the upstream bootloader (MIT license, kept), applied after ferrion-verified-boot.patch, made against upstream commit f3d9261b5fc81418c259c5059f46ee7087e86ed8:
- measured boot on UEFI, through the firmware's EFI_TCG2_PROTOCOL (HashLogExtendEvent), with no new dependency: PCR 7 gets the verified-boot key slot (EV_EFI_VARIABLE_AUTHORITY, variable FerrionBootKey of vendor GUID e569c1f1-7993-453b-8b3a-2109d5d9da22, all zero when verification is off); PCR 8 the boot entry's name (`normal`) and the boot environment without its framebuffer lines (EV_IPL); PCR 9 the manifest (verified boot only), the kernel and the initfs, each after verification and before use (EV_IPL, the event names the file); then EV_SEPARATOR into PCRs 8 and 9. A copy of the TCG event log reaches the kernel as TPM_EVENT_LOG_ADDR and TPM_EVENT_LOG_SIZE in the environment. Without the protocol nothing is measured and the boot is unchanged; when the firmware refuses a measurement the bootloader says so once and boots without further measurements. The BIOS bootloader gets a stub that measures nothing.

